note <a parameter's `fall make <form>` default fills the form's own field falls, as a `make` in a body does, on every backend>

# Item term-self-host-001-1202. check/extend.tree filled a construction's omitted fields from their `fall` in every
# body, but never walked a parameter's default, so `take given, like choice, fall make choice` came out with each field
# at its type's empty value (`fall true` false, `fall <suite.tree>` empty, `fall 7` zero) on TypeScript, Rust, Swift and
# Kotlin alike. test/support/running.tree's `run-text` takes its choice that way, so every suite that ran a program
# through it compiled with `optimize` false (test/compile/arithmetic-masks.tree). A backend whose toolchain is not
# installed is the case's own skip.

load ../support/compiling
  find compile-text
  find compile-choice

load ../support/running
  find backends
  find run-text

load @term/base/test/temp
  find temp-folder

load @term/base/text
  find contains

host program, <form choice\n  link file, like text, fall \<suite.tree\>\n  link optimize, like boolean, fall true\n  link count, like number, fall 7\n\ntask in-body\n  like choice\n  back make choice\n\ntask with-fall\n  take given, like choice, fall make choice\n  like choice\n  back given\n\ntask run\n  like text\n  save a, in-body()\n  save b, with-fall()\n  back \<\{a/optimize\} \{a/file\} \{a/count\} \{b/optimize\} \{b/file\} \{b/count\}\>\n>

test <a defaulted parameter's construction takes each field's own fall>
  take backend, like text
    walk backends()
  host folder, temp-folder(<term-fall-make-fields->)
  host ran, run-text(program, backend, folder, <fall>)
  fork test, is-equal(ran/state, <skipped>)
    hold
      skip <the backend's toolchain is not installed>
  want hold, is-equal(ran/state, <ran>)
  want hold, is-equal(ran/output, <true suite.tree 7 true suite.tree 7>)

# the TypeScript of the default itself, where the empty values showed: the parameter's default record carries the falls
test <the emitted default record is the form's falls>
  host out, compile-text(program, make(compile-choice, bind(file, <fall.tree>), bind(project, <.>), bind(project-env, <node>), bind(env, <node>)))
  want hold, out/ok
  want hold, contains(out/emitted, <given: Choice = \{ file: "suite.tree", optimize: true, count: 7 \}>)
